	(text "The CADENCE-SWANS Payload Controller manages RADFET-based radiation measurements\naboard a 12U CubeSat.\n\nThis board contains:\n\nMicrochip ATSAMV71Q21B-A microcontroller\n5 Varadis RM-VT01-A RADFET channels (1 onboard, 4 external)\nTMUX7208PWR 8:1 analog multiplexer\nADS8695IPWR 18-bit SAR ADC (500 kSPS maximum)\nEverspin MR4A08BCYS35 16-Mbit (2-MiB) nonvolatile MRAM\nI2C temperature, inertial, magnetic, and power monitoring\nUART-to-RS-422 Flight Computer interface\n+3.3V, +5V, and nominal +12V power rails\n\nThe MCU controls each RADFET's enable, R1, and R2 signals; selects analog\nchannels through the TMUX7208; receives 18-bit ADC data over SPI;\nstores measurements in parallel MRAM; and transmits Flight Computer telemetry.\n\n\nPower Requirements per Subsystem\n\nMCU: +3.3V I/O, internally regulated +1.2V core domain\nMRAM: +3.3V\nI2C sensors and INA219 power monitor: +3.3V\nADS8695 ADC: +5V AVDD, +3.3V DVDD\nTMUX7208 analog multiplexer: +12V analog supply, +3.3V GPIO controls\nRS-422 transceiver: +5V\nRADFET channels: +12V; 2mA typical supply current per enabled module\nRADFET disabled supply current: 0.1uA maximum per module\n\nTotal payload input current: 0.5A expected (spacecraft ICD)\nInput power at 0.5A: 4.50W at 9.0V; 6.22W at 12.435V\nFive simultaneously enabled RADFETs: 10mA typical, or 120mW at +12V.\n+3.3V and +5V rail currents vary with MCU operating state and peripheral activity.\n\n\nVBAT - Power Input\n\nSource: Spacecraft BMS/EPS, unregulated\nInput voltage: 9.0V to 12.435V\nExpected input current: 0.5A\nPower input: J14, two VBAT contacts and two GND contacts\nMonitored input: VBAT -> 0.002-ohm shunt -> VBAT_SYS, measured by INA219\nGenerated rails: +3.3V and +5V via LT8612 synchronous buck converters;\nnominal +12V via LT1618 step-up converter\n+12V feedback divider: 909kOhm / 107kOhm, yielding 11.99V nominal\nLT1618 input current sense: 0.1-ohm resistor, approximately 0.5A limit\n+12V rail behavior: the LT1618 boosts lower input voltages to its setpoint.\nWhen VBAT_SYS exceeds the setpoint, the boost-only circuit cannot step down;\nits output can instead be supplied through the inductor and output diode.\n\n\nI2C0 Addresses\n\nLIS2MDL Magnetometer: 0x1E\nINA219AIDCNR Power Monitor: 0x40\nTMP112AIDRLR Temperature Sensor: 0x48\nLSM6DSOXTR Accelerometer/Gyroscope: 0x6A\n\nAll addresses are 7-bit.\n\nAddress pin connections:\nINA219: A0 = GND, A1 = GND\nTMP112: ADD0 = GND\nLSM6DSOX: SA0 = GND; CS = +3.3V for I2C\nLIS2MDL: fixed address 0x1E; CS = +3.3V for I2C"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
